<title>BOTSWANA: TABLE-BARCLAYS HALF YR SHR RISES, DIV UP.</title>
<headline>TABLE-BARCLAYS HALF YR SHR RISES, DIV UP.</headline>
<dateline>GABORONE 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half yr ended June 30 1997</p>
<p>		    (million pula unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (thebe)		   142.99   vs  113.08 (annualised)</p>
<p>    Div (thebe)		    35.00   vs   25.00</p>
<p>    After tax			24.37   vs   19.27</p>
<p>    Net income		     70.79   vs   63.86</p>
<p>    Net interest income	  47.22   vs   37.94</p>
<p>    Other operating income     23.57   vs   25.92</p>
<p>    Bad/doubtful debt charge    0.09   vs    0.68</p>
<p>    Pre-tax			  32.50   vs   25.70</p>
<p>    Tax				 8.12   vs    6.42</p>
<p>Full name: Barclays Bank of Botswana Ltd</p>
<p>Div payable: Sept 8</p>
<p>On register: Aug 29</p>
<p>* Dividend net of 15 percent withholding tax</p>
<p>NOTE - The bank said in a statement the six months had shown a continuing strong performance. The implementation of new computer systems had been completed successfully and the benefits of this together with the implementation of further restructuring projects would be felt in the second half of the year.</p>
<p>The Bank remained strongly capitalised and in a good position to take advantage of new lending opportunities, it said.</p>
<p>-- Gaborone newsroom +267 347182</p>
</text>
